{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the archives was thick with the scent of old parchment and something sharper—the metallic tang of ozone that always preceded a surge in the Ember. Elara traced the spine of the Codex, her fingers trembling slightly. It wasn't just a book; it was a living thing, pulsing with a low, rhythmic heat that matched the thrumming in her own veins.

"It's reacting," she whispered, the sound swallowed by the vast, shadowed silence of the library.

As her skin brushed the leather binding, a spark jumped. It wasn't a painful sting, but a sudden, violent clarity. The runes on the cover began to glow, a deep, molten orange that bled into the cracks of the ancient binding. The Ember wasn't just waking up; it was calling out.", "book_id": "01a029f6-31f3-718b-b014-7d89a73297cb", "chapter": "Chapter I — The Ember Codex", "chapter_id": "01a029f6-335f-74d5-b656-2155f3c0fafe"}, "tier": "A"}

